s, cursor), sleeping in between; the GL thread executes the renderer's commands, swaps and trades buffers with the logic, taking whatever input came so far - a slow message pump (e.g. a mouse hook on Windows making every mouse message cost ~1 ms) no longer stalls frames. Vsync only from the thread that renders (window::apply_vsync); the X11 backend calls XInitThreads and really releases its GLX context; Windows waits for messages with MsgWaitForMultipleObjectsEx. The web build keeps its one main loop.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"phucvinh57/biopass","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:20:04Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"2561514e7854671e7104e91567913a722a6c583c","github_link":"https://github.com/phucvinh57/biopass/commit/2561514e7854671e7104e91567913a722a6c583c","commit_subject":"chore: trim redundant comments and tighten docs (#192)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"quarkusio/quarkus","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:19:37Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"6d64cf3d11e39b9ba1ce8a40dd0b0bf105f22e3a","github_link":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/commit/6d64cf3d11e39b9ba1ce8a40dd0b0bf105f22e3a","commit_subject":"Netty - Read the max direct memory with VM.maxDirectMemory() instead of reflection","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"tursodatabase/turso","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:19:18Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"8193b02478d34478405557402546ac007eebad5f","github_link":"https://github.com/tursodatabase/turso/commit/8193b02478d34478405557402546ac007eebad5f","commit_subject":"Merge 'core/json: keep the stored spelling of JSON5 object keys in fullkey and path' from Ikki Nishihara","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"qLDPCOrg/qLDPC","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:19:09Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"8995b12b87ac145cbed53f738c27f39720a0b74d","github_link":"https://github.com/qLDPCOrg/qLDPC/commit/8995b12b87ac145cbed53f738c27f39720a0b74d","commit_subject":"Rewire circuits into deferred-measurement form (#726)","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"openfootmana